        "original_id": "b653eefe-1095-5a94-aff1-c0fffb9365f8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Hoch Conservatory\n- People: Clara Schumann, Johannes Brahms, Bernhard Cossmann\n- Places: Frankfurt\n- Roles: teacher of cello, faculty\n\nFacts:\n- In 1878, Bernhard Cossmann helped found the Hoch Conservatory in Frankfurt.\n- In 1878, Bernhard Cossmann became the teacher of cello at the Hoch Conservatory.\n- In the late 19th century, Clara Schumann served on the faculty of the Hoch Conservatory.\n- In the late 19th century, the Hoch Conservatory achieved international renown with teachers such as Clara Schumann.\n- Clara Schumann was the first person to perform publicly any work by Johannes Brahms.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
